##DESCRIPTION
##  Use the secant method to estimate a root.
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('secant', 'root')

## DBsubject('Numerical Analysis')
## DBchapter('Rootfinding')
## DBsection('Secant Method')
## Date('2/3/2018')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl',
    'niceTables.pl', 'PGnumericalmacros.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

$a = random(24, 35);

do {
    $x0 = random(1, 5);
    $x1 = random(1, 5);
} until ($x0 != $x1);

$f = Compute("x^2-$a");

@x = @{ secant($f, $x0, $x1)->{iterations} };

$rows1 = [ [ '\(n\)', '\(x_n\)' ] ];
push(@$rows1, [ "\( $_\)", PGML::Format("[_]{$x[$_]}") ]) for (0 .. 6);
$tab1 = LayoutTable(
    $rows1,
    align           => '|c|c|',
    padding         => [ 0.5, 0.5 ],
    horizontalrules => 1
);

BEGIN_PGML

Perform the secant method to find a root of

[`` f(x) =  x^2-[$a]``]

For the first 6 iterations.  Start with [`x_0=[$x0]`] and [`x_1=[$x1]`].

[@ $tab1 @]*

END_PGML

$rows2 = [ [ '\(n\)', '\(x_n\)' ] ];
push(@$rows2, [ "\($_\)", "\($x[$_]\)" ]) for (0 .. 6);
$tab2 = LayoutTable(
    $rows2,
    align           => '|c|c|',
    padding         => [ 0.5, 0.5 ],
    horizontalrules => 1
);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

Recall that the secant method is the iterative formula given by

[``x_{n+1} = x_n - f(x_n)\frac{x_n-x_{n-1}}{f(x_n)-f(x_{n-1})}``]

Using [`x_0=[$x0]`] and [`x_1=[$x1]`] with the function [`f(x)=x^2-[$a]`], then

[``x_{2} = [$x1] - ([$x1]^2-[$a])\frac{[$x1]-[$x0]}{([$x1]^2-[$a])-([$x0]^2-[$a])} = [$x[2]]``]

The next step is

[``x_{3} = [$x[2]] - ([$x[2]]^2-[$a])\frac{[$x[2]]-[$x1]}{([$x[2]]^2-[$a])-([$x1]^2-[$a])} = [$x[3]]``]

and repeating we get the following table:

[@ $tab2 @]*

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
